<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Salt ibn Malik</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 886</span> · Also known as al-Salt ibn Malik al-Kharusi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Salt ibn Malik was Ibadi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> from 851 to 886, one of the longest-reigning rulers of the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">imamate</a>. His rule saw Oman prosper from Gulf trade through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sohar">Sohar</a> and from farming watered by falaj channels, and he sent a fleet to defend <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socotra">Socotra</a>. His deposition in 886 divided Omani scholars into rival schools and led to civil war and Abbasid intervention.</p></div>
